      "end": 8.6,
      "duration": 0.53,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Hi."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.6,
      "end": 10.67,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "In this clip, we're going to discuss the numbering and"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.67,
      "end": 15.73,
      "duration": 5.06,
      "text": "labeling conventions of RNA and of protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 15.73,
      "end": 20.27,
      "duration": 4.54,
      "text": "Here we have a nucleoside triphosphate or NTP."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 20.27,
      "end": 24.11,
      "duration": 3.84,
      "text": "This NTP is numbered on each carbon."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 24.11,
      "end": 28.18,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "And we're going to start here to the right of this oxygen"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 28.18,
      "end": 33.58,
      "duration": 5.4,
      "text": "and label one prime and proceed two prime, three"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 33.58,
      "end": 40.82,
      "duration": 7.24,
      "text": "prime, four prime, and this last, five prime carbon."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 40.82,
      "end": 45.56,
      "duration": 4.74,
      "text": "This means that when we polymerize two or more of"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 45.56,
      "end": 50.63,
      "duration": 5.07,
      "text": "these NTP's to get an RNA chain, it becomes apparent why"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 50.63,
      "end": 53.77,
      "duration": 3.14,
      "text": "one end is labeled five prime and the other end is labeled"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 53.77,
      "end": 55.16,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 55.16,
      "end": 60.2,
      "duration": 5.04,
      "text": "On this end, the extending atom is the five prime carbon."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 60.2,
      "end": 64.269,
      "duration": 4.069,
      "text": "And on this side, the other end, the extending atom is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 64.269,
      "end": 68.04,
      "duration": 3.771,
      "text": "three prime carbon attached to this oxygen."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 68.04,
      "end": 71.12,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "This three prime carbon is where you would attach another"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 71.12,
      "end": 74.34,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "NTP if you would wish to extend this chain."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 74.34,
      "end": 79.07,
      "duration": 4.73,
      "text": "And so we label the ends of RNA five prime to three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 79.07,
      "end": 81.6,
      "duration": 2.53,
      "text": "And RNA is always polymerized in the five prime to the three"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 81.6,
      "end": 82.85,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "prime direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 86.17,
      "end": 91.15,
      "duration": 4.98,
      "text": "Now with our amino acid, we label this end, which is our"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 91.15,
      "end": 96.69,
      "duration": 5.54,
      "text": "amino terminus, as N and this end which is our carboxy"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 96.69,
      "end": 103.74,
      "duration": 7.05,
      "text": "terminus as C. As before, when we polymerize three amino"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 103.74,
      "end": 107.88,
      "duration": 4.14,
      "text": "acids into this short protein chain, I'm going to label this"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 107.88,
      "end": 113.66,
      "duration": 5.78,
      "text": "end which has a protruding amino terminus as N and this"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 113.66,
      "end": 120.37,
      "duration": 6.71,
      "text": "end which has a protruding carboxy terminus as C."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 120.37,
      "end": 124.26,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "So that's how the conventions are in science to label and"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 124.26,
      "end": 126.54,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "number amino acids and proteins."
    },
